// Title: Microsoft VBA For Outlook Addin Loaded Via Outlook
// Sigma ID: 9a0b8719-cd3c-4f0a-90de-765a4cb3f5ed
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-08 | Modified: 2024-03-12
// ATT&CK: execution, T1204.002
// Description: Detects outlvba (Microsoft VBA for Outlook Addin) DLL being loaded by the outlook process
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate macro usage. Add the appropriate filter according to your environment
// References:
//   - https://speakerdeck.com/heirhabarov/hunting-for-persistence-via-microsoft-exchange-server-or-outlook?slide=58
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_office_outlook_outlvba_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\outlook.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\outlvba.dll"
